name: microautophagy
namespace: biological_process
def: "A type of autophagy where cytosolic components are ingested by late endosomes, lysosomes or yeast-type lytic vacuoles by direct invagination of the compartment membrane without prior sequestration into an autophagosome. The engulfing membranes fuse, resulting in the lysosomal delivery of the cargo wrapped in a single membrane derived from the invaginated lysosomal membrane." [PMID:14679207, PMID:15798367, PMID:16973210, PMID:9566964]
